  "body": "## What is missing\n\nPR #2386 added five refusals for a move that turns A in `assets/posts/tormach.cps`.\nThe message of each refusal appears only in the post. No test asserts one of them.\nOne refusal blocks an arc, a canned cycle or a probe move that turns A. It replaces the old \"simultaneous 4-axis\" refusal.\nA later change can remove a refusal, and no test fails.\n\n## Where\n\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps:716`\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps:865`\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps:868`\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps:875`\n- `assets/posts/tormach.cps:903`\n\n## Source\n\nThe read-only Opus review of the merged PR #2386:\nhttps://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/2386#issuecomment-6972209368\n\nThe review read the diff only. It did not build and it ran no test.\n\n## Done when\n\n- One test for each of the five refusals posts a program that causes it.\n- Each test asserts that the post is refused and asserts the message.\n- The tests are in the crate that owns the post engine, with a Gate map line.\n",
